  <data name="HelpQuickStartTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Quick start</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpQuickStartText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Paste a link into the field above (paste button or Ctrl+V), pick resolution, codec and container, optionally enable subtitles or audio-only mode, then press "Download" or Enter. The output folder and speed limit are set below the link field. A list of links can be imported from .txt or dragged into the window.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpQueueTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Queue and playlists</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpQueueText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Multiple links are queued and up to 3 download in parallel (the limit is in Settings). Pause keeps the partial file and resumes later. For playlists enable the "Download playlist" switch — files go into a numbered subfolder. Each queue row offers pause, cancel, retry and opening the folder.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpSubsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Subtitles</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpSubsText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable "Download subtitles" and pick a language ("all" — every language available). "Embed into file" packs subtitles into the container (MP4/MKV work best). Auto-generated subtitles are downloaded along with manual ones.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpConverterTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Converter</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpConverterText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The "Converter" button at the bottom opens the transcoding window: MP4/MKV/MOV and other containers, NVENC/AMF/QSV hardware encoders, quality via CRF or bitrate. The final ffmpeg command is previewed before running. Files can be dragged into the window.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpHotkeysTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keyboard shortcuts</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpHotkeysText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter — add the link to the queue. Esc — cancel the active download (with confirmation). Theme switching — the button in the window title bar.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpTroubleshootingTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Troubleshooting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="HelpTroubleshootingText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If a video fails to download, update yt-dlp (the update check button in the window footer). FFmpeg is required for stream merging and the converter and is downloaded there too. Per-download logs live in %LocalAppData%\VidDownload\logs (button in Settings). Private videos are not supported yet.</value>
  </data>
